 run the ball between the  tackles and outside and be a returned  man a guy that can play in a lot of  snaps and do a lot of different things  for you that guy is now extremely  valuable because now he's one of your  easier best running back he's also one  of your best receivers he's a return man  I think what's a qualm Barkley gives  gives the Giants that that big  playability where it doesn't have to be  it can be anything you toss sweep and  inside run and outside run anything can  score any catch the ball in the  backfield so those the versatility to me  is the biggest change in last how many  years now you're looking for that  versatile guy he's extremely dynamic but  if you've got a group of good running  backs yeah now you just got a good ran  backs you still win with those guys but  you've got a difference maker then  that's worth going to get that guy how  often did recruits think that you were  NC State as opposed to Stanford like  before you guys didn't you put the tree  into the logo just because they thought  you were NC State or Syracuse or is that  true  absolutely I'm not gonna deny it when  when we got here with coach Harbaugh in  2007 I'll never forget it I was I was  the East Coast guy I was I came out of  nine years in the NFL I had never really  been on a recruiting trip so I you know  got the logo on and going to places and  and I walk in and I says hey NC State's  here I mean in Jersey and the case at  Syracuse I know it's so I started  wearing the full Stanford so a big  thankful tonight a thankful to Bob Mosby  at the time to really differentiate our  logo so that we could actually be  recognized but as we all know the  biggest reason why we started  recognizing starting of course of course  well I have two kids who went to USC we  were in South Carolina visiting oh yeah  I know I know they couldn't get into  Stanford David yeah they couldn't get in  there I would have sent them there but  they were in South Carolina with a  hooting the Blowfish concert and they  had their SC stuff on and people said  all you went to South Carolina and the  looks on their face and my kids were  like South Carolina no we went to you  the USC so they faced it as well it's  great to talk to you hopefully we get  some football there and thanks for  joining us we appreciate it  that's David Shaw he's the head coach at  Stanford
 

